329
00:18:40,161 --> 00:18:43,640
At the Natural Toxins Research Center at Texas A&M University

330
00:18:43,641 --> 00:18:48,940
in Kingsville, scientists can't get enough of the stuff.

331
00:18:48,941 --> 00:18:52,380
Their dangerous job is to extract a river of snake venom

332
00:18:52,381 --> 00:18:56,080
that could one day produce medical miracles.

333
00:18:56,081 --> 00:18:58,920
We work with investigators all over the world.

334
00:18:58,921 --> 00:19:02,820
and trying to discover molecules in snake venom

335
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:06,260
that are useful in strokes and heart attacks and cancer

336
00:19:06,360 --> 00:19:08,260
and other medical problems.

337
00:19:08,360 --> 00:19:11,460
Venom is a very complex mixture of thousands

338
00:19:11,560 --> 00:19:12,560
of different molecules.

339
00:19:16,080 --> 00:19:18,980
Extracting the venom from each of the 400 snakes

340
00:19:19,080 --> 00:19:20,180
is not for the cowardly.

341
00:19:23,520 --> 00:19:27,180
It requires scheduled hand milkings, a job you definitely

342
00:19:27,181 --> 00:19:30,080
